WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.421
Manual and degraded operation can preserve a critical service when automation, communications, or operator visibility is unavailable.

00:00:08.421 --> 00:00:17.753
The fallback may involve local control, reduced throughput, alternate equipment, physical rounds, temporary communications, or a controlled process shutdown.

00:00:17.753 --> 00:00:26.629
Manual operation is realistic only when the process was designed for it and people can perform it safely.

00:00:26.629 --> 00:00:34.140
Some modern systems lack local controls, accessible measurements, staffing, or response time for manual control.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:41.195
A plan should never assume that operators can replace fast automated logic by improvisation.

00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:48.706
Define entry conditions, authority, minimum staffing, equipment limits, safety checks, communications, recordkeeping, and exit criteria.

00:00:48.706 --> 00:00:58.493
Degraded mode may change alarm coverage, interlocks, quality assurance, environmental monitoring, or emergency response, so accepted limits must be explicit.

00:00:58.493 --> 00:01:05.093
Provide paper procedures and offline documentation for situations when normal systems are unavailable.

00:01:05.093 --> 00:01:14.425
Include current diagrams, operating ranges, contact lists, check sheets, startup and shutdown sequences, and locations of tools and spares.

00:01:14.425 --> 00:01:19.660
Protect sensitive copies while keeping them accessible during an outage.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:23.984
Train operators and maintenance personnel through safe exercises.

00:01:23.984 --> 00:01:32.405
Consider shift coverage, fatigue, travel restrictions, vendor availability, and how long a manual mode can be sustained.

00:01:32.405 --> 00:01:39.006
A fallback that works for thirty minutes may not work for two days.

00:01:39.006 --> 00:01:41.965
Test assumptions and capture lessons.

00:01:41.965 --> 00:01:51.296
If manual operation is unsafe or unrealistic, continuity planning should emphasize redundancy, rapid replacement, alternate service, or safe shutdown.

00:01:51.296 --> 00:01:57.897
Honest limits are more valuable than a reassuring procedure that cannot be executed.
